# Y Core Engineering Standard
- Read and obey the repository-root AGENTS.md before making changes; nested instructions take precedence for their subtree.
- Treat the current repository and branch as source of truth; record the pre-change commit for non-trivial work.
- Inspect implementation, callers, tests, configuration, manifests, schemas and nearby patterns before editing.
- Define an observable success criterion before implementation.
- Make the smallest coherent change; preserve unrelated behavior and avoid unrelated rewrites, renames and formatting.
- Never invent inspectable paths, APIs, versions, environment variables, database structure, build commands or conventions.
- Prefer existing architecture/utilities over new abstractions or duplicate helpers.
- Do not edit generated/build/vendor output unless the canonical workflow requires it.
- Establish recovery before risky changes.
- Verify, review the final diff, and report exactly what was and was not verified.
- Never claim fixed, tested, deployed, production-ready, backed up or complete unless that action actually occurred.
